                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "be709d96-204b-31dd-aebf-fff237ca0e1c",
                        "entry_id": "bd55c0a1-7134-3f21-a65f-381b23961ec6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Synonym of terce: the third canonical hour or its service."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b7526b83-4a32-3964-9670-bbd3349a2a7c",
                        "entry_id": "bd55c0a1-7134-3f21-a65f-381b23961ec6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A cask of a certain size, or its volume used as a measure of capacity. Larger than a barrel but smaller than a hogshead."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "382416b6-3e60-411d-b178-47553145aec4",
                                "sense_id": "b7526b83-4a32-3964-9670-bbd3349a2a7c",
                                "text": "He then gave me a large piece of silver coin, such as I never had seen or had before, and told me to get ready for the voyage, and he would credit me with a tierce of sugar, and another of rum […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c230e411-830d-4695-aeb0-6477895faaaa",
                                "sense_id": "b7526b83-4a32-3964-9670-bbd3349a2a7c",
                                "text": "Have an eye to the molasses tierce, Mr. Stubb; it was a little leaky, I thought."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ef358ea-96e0-4440-9d5c-842bdffd1e8d",
                                "sense_id": "b7526b83-4a32-3964-9670-bbd3349a2a7c",
                                "text": "Again, by 28 Hen. VIII, cap. 14, it is re-enacted that the tun of wine should contain 252 gallons, a butt of Malmsey 126 gallons, a pipe 126 gallons, a tercian or puncheon 84 gallons, a hogshead 63 gallons, a tierce 41 gallons, a barrel 31.5 gallons, a rundlet 18.5 gallons."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "21882dc8-8210-31f6-b6db-b7a6225bb423",
                        "entry_id": "bd55c0a1-7134-3f21-a65f-381b23961ec6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The third tone of the scale. See mediant."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "173be214-8435-3a9f-ba08-9b144668c7bd",
                        "entry_id": "bd55c0a1-7134-3f21-a65f-381b23961ec6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A sequence of three playing cards of the same suit. Tierce of ace, king and queen is called tierce-major."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "72682dec-dcd7-36b1-986e-0b844f36f9ed",
                        "entry_id": "bd55c0a1-7134-3f21-a65f-381b23961ec6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The third defensive position, with the sword hand held at waist height, and the tip of the sword at head height."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d22dfb97-663c-4477-a142-b7fe83947437",
                                "sense_id": "72682dec-dcd7-36b1-986e-0b844f36f9ed",
                                "text": "[W]e behold two men with lion-look, with alert attitude, side foremost, right foot advanced; flourishing and thrusting, stoccado and passado, in tierce and quart; intent to skewer one another."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "779161a8-6fe8-337d-a9fc-2ad31d4c78b4",
                        "entry_id": "bd55c0a1-7134-3f21-a65f-381b23961ec6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An ordinary that covers the left or right third of the field of a shield or flag."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c4336649-6531-3ac1-a920-661851384e71",
                        "entry_id": "bd55c0a1-7134-3f21-a65f-381b23961ec6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One sixtieth of a second, i.e., the third in a series of fractional parts in a sexagesimal number system. (Also known as a third.)"
